<title>FRANCE: Eastern Sugar buys 40 pct of Hungary's Kaba.</title>
<headline>Eastern Sugar buys 40 pct of Hungary's Kaba.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eastern Sugar, a company owned by French Saint Louis and British Tate &amp; Lyle, has bought 40 percent of the capital of Hungarian Sucriere de Kaba to take its stake to 74.6 percent, the Generale Sucriere subsidiary of Saint-Louis said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the stake was bought from Hungary's APVR privatisation agency but did not give price details.</p>
<p>&quot;This takes its (Eastern Sugar) stake in the biggest sugar firm in the country to 74.6 percent,&quot; the statement said.</p>
</text>
